From king at harvard.edu  Tue Aug  2 15:04:13 2005
From: king at harvard.edu (Gary King)
Date: Tue, 2 Aug 2005 15:04:13 -0400 (EDT)
Subject: [amelia] Commands for Imputing Dichotomous Variables in AMELIA
In-Reply-To: <4DE4D12462085646A7FC4B62FC26430901EBE920@ssa08.ssa.ad.uchicago.edu>
References: <4DE4D12462085646A7FC4B62FC26430901EBE920@ssa08.ssa.ad.uchicago.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.63.0508021502300.26301@w3.hmdc.harvard.edu>


Experiments seem to indicate that for imputation, you can use the normal 
model underlying Amelia, even though you wouldn't want to use it for the 
analysis model.  if you choose options appropriately, Amelia will 
dichotomize the resulting simulations for convenience of subsequent 
analysis.  But if that's not necessary for your analysis model, then using 
the continuously imputed variable should work fine.

Gary King

